<report>
<title>Linearity with replicates of Y</title>
<table>
<tr><th>Source of variation</th><th>SSq</th><th>DF</th><th>MSq</th><th>VR</th><th></th></tr>
<tr><td>Due to regression</td><td>@{reg_ssq:roundu}</td><td>@reg_df</td><td>@{reg_msq:roundu}</td><td>@{reg_vr:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{reg_p:pval}</pval></td></tr>
<tr><td>Deviation of x means</td><td>@{dev_ssq:roundu}</td><td>@dev_df</td><td>@{dev_msq:roundu}</td><td>@{dev_vr:roundu}</td><td><pval>@{dev_p:pval}</pval></td></tr>
<tr><td>Within x residual</td><td>@{res_ssq:roundu}</td><td>@res_df</td><td>@{res_msq:roundu}</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>Total</td><td>@{tot_ssq:roundu}</td><td>@tot_df</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
</table>

<p>Regression slope is <b>@reg</b>significant<br />
Assumption of linearity <b>@lin</b>supported</p>
</report>
